-- title:
--   §4.4 Step 2, p. 19 — (E_{r^n,σ}[f_i])_n is a martingale converging P_σ-a.s. to f_i
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a stochastic game, $\sigma$ a strategy profile, $s$ an initial state and $i$ a player, and let $\mathcal F^n$ be the σ-algebra generated by the histories of stage $n$. The process $\big(\mathbf E_\sigma[f_i\mid\mathcal F^n]\big)_{n\in\mathbb N}$, realized as $r\mapsto\mathbf E_{r^n,\sigma}[f_i]$, is a martingale under $\mathbf P_\sigma=\mathbf P_{s,\sigma}$, and
--   $$\mathbf E_{r^n,\sigma}[f_i]\ \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\ f_i(r)\qquad\text{for }\mathbf P_\sigma\text{-almost every run }r.$$
--
--   In the proof of Theorem 4.9 this is applied to $\sigma=\sigma^*$ to find a stage $n_1$ after which, with probability more than $2/3$, the expected payoff in the subgame at the current history is $\delta$-close to the realized payoff (Eq. (14)).
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper states this for $\sigma^*$; nothing of $\sigma^*$ is used, so it is stated for every profile. The process is $n\mapsto$ `payoff G σ n (frestrictLe n r) i`, which is the paper's $\mathbf E_{r^{n+1},\sigma}[f_i]$ (Lean index $n$ is paper stage $n+1$), adapted to `Filtration.piLE` (the paper's $\mathcal F^{n+1}$). Identifying it with a version of $\mathbf E_\sigma[f_i\mid\mathcal F^{n+1}]$ is part of what is to be proved.
-- source:
--   Flesch & Solan, Stochastic Games with General Payoff Functions, arXiv:2208.12096v1, p. 19, §4.4 Step 2, first sentence and Eq. (14); F^n and C(h) on p. 17

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GenPayoffSG_Solvable_Game

namespace GenPayoffSG.Solvable

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology

variable {I S : Type} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I] [Nonempty I]
  [Countable S] [Nonempty S] {A : I → Type}
  [∀ i, Fintype (A i)] [∀ i, Nonempty (A i)] [∀ i, DecidableEq (A i)]

theorem step2_martingale (G : Game I S A) (σ : Profile G) (s : S) (i : I) :
    Martingale (fun n r => payoff G σ n (Preorder.frestrictLe n r) i) Filtration.piLE
        (playMeasure G σ 0 (initHist s)) ∧
      ∀ᵐ r ∂(playMeasure G σ 0 (initHist s)),
        Tendsto (fun n => payoff G σ n (Preorder.frestrictLe n r) i) atTop (𝓝 (G.f i r)) := by sorry

end GenPayoffSG.Solvable
